The following occurred the other day on my Mac (SE/30, 4meg, it happens
even without any INITs and cdevs except SUM Partition)

1) save a game
2) duplicate the save file
3) run the copy
4) save the game over the original save file
5) restart the (resaved) save file
6) Nethack reports that the 'dungeon is not as I remember it', attempts
   to boot me off but doesn't even get that far because the system reports
   that it has quit unexpectedly (out of memory). I regret that I haven't
   tried this under Singlefinder. Occasionally (impossible to duplicate
   accurately) the Finder reports that it is closing window "" a few times
   before it crashes (this is after the out-of-memory error)

BTW I'm running System 6.0.3.

Also there seem to be problems when switching out of Nethack and moving around
the little iconized window. It's nice (I like the Sun windowing systems myself)
but it crashes sometimes. Can't figure out exactly how to make it do it.

And lastly an interface proposition:
The Mac OS (the Finder spcifically) lets you drag around background windows
without moving them to the foreground by holding down the funny-looking
command key during the drag operation. Perhaps NetHack could implement this
for those of us who use MultiFinder.
Great game guys!
